ant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYASHITA HIROHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI KAZUSHIGE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JAPAN ENERGY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYASHITA, HIROHITO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, KAZUSHIGE</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYASHITA HIROHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI KAZUSHIGE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYASHITA, HIROHITO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, KAZUSHIGE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of manufacturing a Co-Ti alloy sputtering target containing not more than 100 ppm of oxygen and having a grain size of not larger than 50  mu m, comprising forming a Co-Ti alloy ingot by vacuum-melting and casting a Co-Ti alloy containing 0.5 to 20 wt.% of Ti, and then hot-working the ingot.  The Co-Ti alloy sputtering target containing the above small amount oxygen is useful for forming a sputtering thin film which is excellent in film-forming uniformity and has few particles.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un procédé de fabrication d'une cible pour pulvérisation cathodique, constituée d'un alliage Co-Ti ne contenant pas plus de 100 ppm d'oxygène et ayant une taille de grains inférieure à 50  mu m. Ledit procédé consiste à former un lingot en alliage Co-Ti en effectuant la fusion sous vide puis le moulage d'un alliage Co-Ti contenant 0,5 à 20 % en poids de titane, puis à travailler ledit lingot à chaud. Cette cible pour pulvérisation cathodique constituée d'un alliage Co-Ti et contenant la faible quantité d'oxygène mentionnée ci-dessus permet la fabrication par pulvérisation cathodique d'un film fin qui présente une excellente uniformité et contient peu de particules.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>